if you're worried that the PlayStation  4's lifecycle is coming to an end you  can rest easy despite the upcoming  release of Sony's more powerful  PlayStation 4 codenamed neo this doesn't  mean that the ps4's life cycle will end  any earlier Shuhei Yoshida president of  Sony's worldwide studios said in an  interview well no ps4 is ps4 you know  the new high-end ps4 is still a ps4 so  the lifecycle is not going to be any  shorter it sounds like the neo in the  ps4 will complement each other the neo  will be the pricier and more high-end  console whereas the standard model will  be more affordable Yoshida's comments  match up with what playstation president  andrew house said this month when he  confirmed that a more powerful ps4 is in  development he said quote it is intended  to sit alongside and complement the  standard ps4 we will be selling both  versions throughout the lifecycle the  Neo currently doesn't have a release  date but a report said that it would  arrive this year there's no word yet on  a price but we'll be sure to let you  know as soon as we find out for more  news and all sorts of new console  goodness stay tuned to gamespot com  you
 

